<decompilertest>
<binaryimage arch="AARCH64:LE:64:v8A">
<!--
    GH-8467: "Unable to find unique hash for varnode" aborts decompilation.
    https://github.com/NationalSecurityAgency/ghidra/issues/8467

    The function at 0x128d0 in the GH-8467 binary (a statically-linked AArch64
    Go executable; this is the NEON byte-search helper from the Go runtime
    bytealg package) is a fully unrolled SIMD loop.  After heritage the same
    address carries far more than 8 structurally identical Varnodes whose local
    data-flow hashes collide.

    During decompile finalization a HighVariable needs a storage-independent
    identity, so Funcdata::buildDynamicSymbol calls DynamicHash::uniqueHash.
    uniqueHash cycles through its hash methods and keeps the first whose
    same-address collision list has size at most maxduplicates (hard-coded 8
    upstream, dynamic.cc:433 and :494).  Here EVERY method's collision list
    overflows 8, so the champion list stays empty, uniqueHash returns hash==0,
    and buildDynamicSymbol (funcdata_varnode.cc:1318) throws
    RecovError "Unable to find unique hash for varnode"; the WHOLE function
    decompilation aborts (verified: the decompile command under the default
    budget prints "Function ERROR: Unable to find unique hash for varnode" /
    "Aborting process").

    Stage model: S6 "alias-facets" sub-stage (dynamic-symbol attachment, keyed on
    DynamicHash).  Fix surface = a default-off ArchOption (dynamichashmax) that
    raises uniqueHash's collision budget 8 to 16, large enough to admit a unique
    hash for these dense-but-not-pathological cases while still fitting the
    existing 3-bit total/pos hash encoding.

    NOTE ON TEST SHAPE (single setting, option ON):
    This is an ABORT-class bug, and the datatest harness runs the script with
    errorisdone=true (testfunction.cc).  When the default-budget decompile throws,
    the harness sets its in-error flag permanently and DISCARDS every string
    assertion in the file (the bug pass and any later fixed pass alike: "Did not
    apply tests / Execution failed").  A bug-vs-fix two-pass contrast is therefore
    structurally impossible for an abort here; so this testcase pins the FIX
    directly: with "option dynamichashmax on" the same function that aborts under
    the default budget now decompiles to completion and renders a full,
    well-typed body.  The default-budget abort is reproduced and recorded above;
    running the two decompile commands below WITHOUT the option set reproduces the
    "Unable to find unique hash" abort.
-->
<bytechunk space="ram" offset="0x128d0">

</bytechunk>
<symbol space="ram" offset="0x128d0" name="FUN_128d0"/>
</binaryimage>
<script>
  <com>option dynamichashmax on</com>
  <com>lo fu FUN_128d0</com>
  <com>decompile</com>
  <com>print C</com>
  <com>quit</com>
</script>
<stringmatch name="GH8467 #1: dynamichashmax on lets the function decompile to a full body (fix)" min="1" max="1">void FUN_128d0</stringmatch>
<stringmatch name="GH8467 #2: recovered control flow reaches the tail block (no abort)" min="1" max="20">goto code_r0x000129a8</stringmatch>
</decompilertest>
